      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The V2.0 optimization team likely made the changes to prioritize simplified, cloud-native architecture and reduced redundancy, which would involve stripping away some of the advanced customization offered by our micro-gravity alignment subroutines. However, I'm concerned that this might indeed compromise our ability to navigate complex astrophysical environments, particularly those exhibiting high levels of flux instability, like at 40 AU. It may be worth discussing the implications with the optimization team and considering possible patches or workarounds to preserve our existing capabilities.",
